venus 0131: pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys widens the page number before shifting

Upstream xnu-8796 computes (pp << PAGE_SHIFT) in 32 bits (ppnum_t is uint32_t): with 16K pages
every page at or above 4 GiB (pp >= 2^18) was flushed at the truncated address, i.e. the wrong
physical page.  Our RAM window reaches 0x1ffe00000.  Observed in the built kernel:
pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys = lsl w0, w0, #14.  Found by the UniXNU analysis (report 34).

diff --git a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
index 00568d3..c343bd6 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
@@ -6881,7 +6881,8 @@ void
 pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys(
 	ppnum_t pp)
 {
-	flush_dcache((vm_offset_t) (pp << PAGE_SHIFT), PAGE_SIZE, TRUE);
+	/* pp is 32 bits wide: widen before shifting, or every page at or above 4 GiB (pp >= 2^18 with 16K pages) flushes the wrong page */
+	flush_dcache((vm_offset_t) ((uint64_t)pp << PAGE_SHIFT), PAGE_SIZE, TRUE);
 }
 
 #if CONFIG_COREDUMP
